,"modu":{"name":"Modu Atelier","type":"Made-to-order furniture · Qualified project enquiries","tone":"#29241F","intro":"Your furniture website should do more than show attractive sofas. It should help each visitor understand the scale of a piece, find the finish they like and tell you what they need before starting a custom order.","potential":"When dimensions, finishes and selected pieces travel together in one enquiry, your first client conversation can focus on what is feasible. A saved shortlist and clear measurement steps give visitors reasons to return and finish their brief.","wins":[["Let visitors shop by room, not guesswork","Each piece has its own proportions, selectable widths, finish choices and feet. Visitors can explore options without having to send an open-ended message first."],["Reduce the fear of buying the wrong size","The room-fit helper invites customers to compare width and doorway clearances before they enquire. A real business would confirm shipping access and product dimensions."],["Keep the details together","Visitors can save configurations, choose up to four fabric tones and send one summary with size, material and room details. You receive a more useful starting brief."]],"references":[["Interior Define","https://swatches.interiordefine.com/","Interior Define makes exploring free fabric swatches and material filters approachable. Your site could keep swatch choices directly beside dimensions and the customer's saved design."],["BenchMade Modern","https://benchmademodern.com/collections/sofas","BenchMade Modern clearly presents silhouette, size and custom upholstery as a three-step choice and offers concierge help. Your version brings a room-fit check into the decision before customers become overwhelmed."],["Joybird","https://joybird.com/samples/","Joybird offers swatch kits to make fabric decisions easier. Your site can carry those selected swatches into the same enquiry as the chosen furniture and measurements."]],"platforms":[["Webflow","A great fit for an editorial collection, refined motion, CMS-driven product pages and integrated enquiry workflows."],["Wix Studio","An approachable option for a custom furniture portfolio, swatch enquiries and owner-managed collections."],["WordPress","Useful when you want a large product catalogue, WooCommerce integration and flexible quoting features."]],"status":"Original portfolio concept. Products and photos are illustrative; no manufacturer, real prices, shipping promises or orders are claimed."}
